 "_about": "Review ledger for the annotation of the 15 released sheets. The annotation files are not edited; scoring/score.py applies this ledger on top of them, for every system alike. \"fixes\" are annotated shapes that the drawing shows to be something else: each is removed from the object annotation, or relabelled. \"added\" are windows the annotators missed, added as upright boxes. \"not_scored\" are boxes in which a delivered object of the named class that matches nothing is neither found nor false, because the drawing shows such an object there and the annotation does not mark it separately. Boxes are [x0, y0, x1, y1] in the pixel frame of the annotation; a fix names the annotated shape by its class and its bounding box (within one pixel). Every entry was checked against the drawing by the benchmark owner. The ledger changes the object annotation only: areas and walls are scored on the annotation as exported.",
